  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Orange Talks - Engaging man on the fight against women&apos;s violence.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In line with the Netherlands strategy to promote women&apos;s rights and gender equality, the embassy will promote an Orange Talks on engaging man to promote gender equality.
Activity is aligned with the Dutch policy which considers engaging men and boys a critical, strategic component of its efforts to combat gender-based violence (GBV) and achieve gender equality, integrating this approach into both domestic policy and foreign policy. 
The Orange Talks is an event led by a man only panel and with an audience of mostly man. The initiative aims to promote a safe space for men to discuss on how to engage man on the fight against gender-based violence.
This will be a part of a series of events mainly focus on discussing the challenges and solutions for the male engagement and promoting positive masculinities.</narrative>
  </description>
